1
00:00:07,480 --> 00:00:09,860
A car has a 52 litre fuel tank.

2
00:00:09,910 --> 00:00:13,000
The driver fills 0.4 of the tank.

3
00:00:13,050 --> 00:00:17,060
Without a calculator, how many litres is 0.4 times 52?

4
00:00:17,110 --> 00:00:20,870
Pause the video and work it out.

5
00:00:20,920 --> 00:00:24,330
Work out 4 times 52, which is 208.

6
00:00:24,380 --> 00:00:28,810
0.4 is 4 divided by 10, so divide 208 by 10.

7
00:00:28,860 --> 00:00:31,000
The answer is 20.8 litres.

8
00:00:32,050 --> 00:00:35,290
Estimate to check: 0.4 times 50 is 20.

9
00:00:35,340 --> 00:00:36,360
Close.

10
00:00:36,410 --> 00:00:39,840
Remember: 0.4 is 4 divided by 10.

11
00:00:39,890 --> 00:00:43,550
And 0.15 is 15 divided by 100.

12
00:00:43,600 --> 00:00:45,430
Multiply the whole numbers.

13
00:00:45,480 --> 00:00:48,650
Then count the decimal places in both numbers.

14
00:00:48,700 --> 00:00:51,990
The answer has that many decimal places.

15
00:00:52,040 --> 00:00:52,830
Your turn.

16
00:00:52,880 --> 00:00:54,840
Work out 0.3 times 0.15.

17
00:00:54,890 --> 00:00:58,490
Pause the video and try it.

18
00:00:58,540 --> 00:01:00,080
3 times 15 is 45.

19
00:01:00,130 --> 00:01:06,330
There are 3 decimal places altogether: one in 0.3, and two in 0.15.

20
00:01:06,380 --> 00:01:09,030
So the answer is 0.045.

21
00:01:09,080 --> 00:01:16,490
To divide by a decimal, multiply both numbers by the same power of 10, until the divisor is a whole number.

22
00:01:16,540 --> 00:01:18,930
The answer does not change.

23
00:01:18,980 --> 00:01:26,090
7.56 divided by 0.09 is the same as 756 divided by 9, which is 84.

24
00:01:26,140 --> 00:01:31,780
Dividing a positive number by a number between 0 and 1 makes it bigger.

25
00:01:31,830 --> 00:01:33,150
Here is the method.

26
00:01:33,200 --> 00:01:35,720
Step 1: estimate the answer.

27
00:01:35,770 --> 00:01:43,070
Step 2: to multiply, multiply as whole numbers, then put back the total number of decimal places.

28
00:01:43,120 --> 00:01:49,640
Step 3: to divide, multiply both numbers by 10, or 100, until the divisor is whole.

29
00:01:49,690 --> 00:01:51,140
Then divide.

30
00:01:51,190 --> 00:01:54,290
Step 4: compare with your estimate.

31
00:01:54,340 --> 00:01:57,710
Work out 1.44 divided by 0.012.

32
00:01:57,760 --> 00:02:04,680
Multiply both by 1,000: 1,440 divided by 12, which is 120.

33
00:02:04,730 --> 00:02:05,480
Your turn.

34
00:02:05,530 --> 00:02:08,370
Work out negative 16 divided by 0.4.

35
00:02:08,420 --> 00:02:11,530
Pause and work it out.

36
00:02:11,580 --> 00:02:18,310
Multiply both by 10: negative 160 divided by 4, which is negative 40.

37
00:02:18,360 --> 00:02:20,700
Work out 2.4 times 0.35.

38
00:02:20,750 --> 00:02:22,590
24 times 35 is 840.

39
00:02:22,640 --> 00:02:29,140
There are 3 decimal places, so the answer is 0.840, which is 0.84.

40
00:02:29,190 --> 00:02:32,030
Estimate: 2 times 0.4 is 0.8.

41
00:02:32,080 --> 00:02:33,170
Close.

42
00:02:33,220 --> 00:02:35,520
Mia works out 0.2 times 0.3.

43
00:02:35,570 --> 00:02:37,750
Which line is wrong?

44
00:02:37,800 --> 00:02:38,950
Line 2 is wrong.

45
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:42,890
There are 2 decimal places altogether, not 1.

46
00:02:42,940 --> 00:02:45,650
So the answer is 0.06.

47
00:02:45,700 --> 00:02:49,570
Cheese costs 12 dollars 40 per kilogram.

48
00:02:49,620 --> 00:02:56,490
0.75 of a kilogram costs 12.40 times 0.75, which is 9 dollars 30.

49
00:02:56,540 --> 00:02:57,890
One last question.

50
00:02:57,940 --> 00:02:59,910
Work out 3 divided by 0.5.

51
00:02:59,960 --> 00:03:03,400
Pause the video and answer.

52
00:03:03,450 --> 00:03:07,180
Multiply both by 10: 30 divided by 5 is 6.

53
00:03:07,230 --> 00:03:09,880
There are 6 halves in 3.

54
00:03:09,930 --> 00:03:12,570
To remember: estimate first.

55
00:03:12,620 --> 00:03:17,200
When multiplying, count the decimal places in both numbers.

56
00:03:17,250 --> 00:03:21,860
When dividing, scale both numbers to make the divisor whole.

57
00:03:21,910 --> 00:03:26,870
Dividing by a number less than 1 makes a positive number bigger.

58
00:03:26,920 --> 00:03:32,030
Great work! Now practise lesson 3.2 on Camday.
